# Neo Sampler parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5, Neo Sampler). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoSampler
namespace NeoBuzz.Sampler
class NeoSamplerMachine
tracks 16
summary Sampler that plays the song's waves (wavetable slots, from wave_import) and built-in samples: 16 zones by key and velocity range, each with its wave, root, tune, level, pan, start, end, loop with crossfade, gate or one-shot, reverse and a choke group; a wave slot's layers split its keys by root or alternate round robin; amp and filter envelopes, velocity to level and filter, pitch bend; Kit mode puts zone n on key Kit base + n − 1 as a one-shot drum. Use it for drum kits, sampled instruments and one-shots.

group Play
Mode        "Mode"          0 1    0    enum Instrument Kit             | Instrument: each zone plays the notes in its key and velocity ranges, tuned from its root; Kit: zone n plays key Kit base + n − 1 at its own pitch, one-shot (key and velocity ranges, root, loop and trigger aside)
    how Chooses Instrument (zones play by key and velocity range, tuned from their root) or Kit (each zone gets its own key, one-shot).
    sound Instrument mode plays a sample as a melodic instrument, and Kit mode turns zones into a drum pad set.
KitBase     "Kit base"      0 112  36   int 0 note                      | The key zone 1 plays in Kit mode (36 = C2, General MIDI's kick: zone 3 is D2 the snare, 7 F#2 the closed hat, 11 A#2 the open hat); the others follow a semitone apart
    how Sets the key that plays zone 1 in Kit mode, from 0 to 112; the other zones follow a semitone apart.
    sound Move it to line the kit up with the keys or pads you play it from.
Polyphony   "Polyphony"     1 32   32   int 0                           | Voices that sound at once (each zone a note plays takes one); past it a new voice takes the quietest released one, else the oldest, fading it out in 3 ms
    how Sets how many voices can sound at once, from 1 to 32.
    sound More voices let long samples and chords overlap, and fewer make new notes cut off the quietest older ones.
BendRange   "Bend range"    0 24   2    int 0 st                        | Pitch bend range
    how Sets how far the pitch bend wheel moves the pitch, from 0 to 24 semitones.
    sound A small range gives expressive nudges, and a large one gives big sweeps.
VelAmp      "Vel → amp"     0 1000 700  pct                             | How much velocity sets the level: the gain is velocity^(2 × this) (100 %: velocity 64 is −12 dB; 0 %: every note at full level)
    how Sets how strongly note velocity changes the loudness, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound High values make dynamics audible, and 0 % makes all notes equally loud.
VelXfade    "Vel crossfade" 0 64   0    int 0                           | Zones whose velocity ranges meet crossfade (equal power) over this many velocity steps around the boundary instead of switching; 0 switches
    how Sets how many velocity steps zones crossfade over where their velocity ranges meet, from 0 to 64.
    sound Zero switches abruptly between layers, and higher values blend them smoothly as you play harder.
Volume      "Volume"        0 720  600  db -60 12 inf                   | Output level
    how Sets the output level of the sampler, from -60 to +12 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to place the instrument in the mix without changing its tone.

group Amp env
AmpA        "Amp attack"    0 1000 0    time 0.0005 20                  | Attack time (the shortest, 0.5 ms, keeps a note starting mid-wave from clicking)
    how Sets how long the loudness envelope takes to rise at the start of a note, from 0.5 ms to 20 seconds.
    sound Short attacks keep the sample's own start, and long ones fade it in slowly like a pad.
AmpD        "Amp decay"     0 1000 700  time 0.0005 20                  | Decay time (to −60 dB of the way to sustain)
    how Sets how long the loudness envelope takes to fall to its sustain level, from 0.5 ms to 20 seconds.
    sound Short decays make a plucky note, and long ones let it ring down slowly.
AmpS        "Amp sustain"   0 1000 1000 pct                             | Sustain level
    how Sets the loudness the note holds while the key stays down, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound A low sustain makes the note die away even when held, and 100 % keeps it at full volume.
AmpR        "Amp release"   0 1000 538  time 0.0005 20                  | Release time after the note ends (to −60 dB)
    how Sets how long the note takes to fade out after the key is released, from 0.5 ms to 20 seconds.
    sound Short releases stop the note cleanly, and long ones let it fade out after you let go.

group Filter
FType       "Filter"        0 4    0    enum Off LP_24 LP_12 BP HP      | Filter on every voice: off, ladder low-pass 24 or 12 dB/oct, state-variable band-pass or high-pass
    how Chooses the filter on every voice: off, a 24 or 12 dB low-pass, band-pass or high-pass.
    sound The low-pass darkens the sample, the band-pass makes it thin and nasal, and the high-pass removes its body.
FCutoff     "Cutoff"        0 1000 1000 freq 20 20000                   | Cutoff
    how Sets the filter cutoff frequency, from 20 Hz to 20 kHz.
    sound Low values make the sound dark and muffled, and high values open it up.
FReso       "Resonance"     0 1000 0    pct                             | Resonance (the ladder self-oscillates at the top)
    how Sets the filter resonance, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound More resonance puts a whistling peak at the cutoff, and the top turns it into a ringing tone.
FEnv        "Filter env"    0 1000 500  bip                             | Filter envelope amount (±6 octaves)
    how Sets how much the filter envelope moves the cutoff, up to six octaves either way.
    sound Positive amounts make each note open and close, and negative ones sweep the other way.
FKey        "Key track"     0 1000 0    pct                             | Cutoff follows the keyboard around C4 (100 %: an octave per octave)
    how Sets how much the cutoff follows the note pitch, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound At 100 % the brightness stays even over the keyboard, and lower values make high notes duller.
FVel        "Filter vel"    0 1000 0    pct                             | Softer notes close the filter (up to 3 octaves at the lowest velocity)
    how Sets how much soft notes close the filter, up to three octaves.
    sound Harder playing sounds brighter, which makes the instrument feel more expressive.

group Filter env
FltA        "Flt attack"    0 1000 0    time 0.0005 20                  | Attack time
    how Sets how long the filter envelope takes to rise, from 0.5 ms to 20 seconds.
    sound Short attacks open the filter at once, and long ones make the brightness swell in.
FltD        "Flt decay"     0 1000 520  time 0.0005 20                  | Decay time
    how Sets how long the filter envelope takes to fall to its sustain level, from 0.5 ms to 20 seconds.
    sound Short decays make a quick wah-like snap, and long ones a slow sweep down.
FltS        "Flt sustain"   0 1000 0    pct                             | Sustain level
    how Sets the level the filter envelope holds while the key stays down, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound A high sustain keeps the filter open while a key is held, and a low one lets it close.
FltR        "Flt release"   0 1000 538  time 0.0005 20                  | Release time
    how Sets how long the filter envelope takes to fall back after the key is released, from 0.5 ms to 20 seconds.
    sound Short releases close the filter at once, and long ones let the tone fade out.

group Zone 1
Z1Wave    "Z1 wave"      0 254 1    int 0 wave            | Zone 1's wave: 0 off, 1–200 a slot of the song's wavetable (wave_import), 201 on a built-in sample (the manual lists them)
    how Chooses the sound zone 1 plays: off, a wave slot of the song, or a built-in sample.
    sound The wave is the raw material of the zone; each slot or sample has its own character.
Z1KeyLo   "Z1 key low"   0 127 0    int 0 note             | Zone 1: the lowest key it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the lowest key zone 1 plays in Instrument mode.
    sound Together with the high key it decides which part of the keyboard triggers this zone.
Z1KeyHi   "Z1 key high"  0 127 127  int 0 note             | Zone 1: the highest key it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the highest key zone 1 plays in Instrument mode.
    sound Together with the low key it decides which part of the keyboard triggers this zone.
Z1VelLo   "Z1 vel low"   1 127 1    int 0                  | Zone 1: the lowest velocity it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the lowest velocity zone 1 responds to in Instrument mode.
    sound Zones with different velocity ranges give a soft layer and a hard layer on the same keys.
Z1VelHi   "Z1 vel high"  1 127 127  int 0                  | Zone 1: the highest velocity it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the highest velocity zone 1 responds to in Instrument mode.
    sound Zones with different velocity ranges give a soft layer and a hard layer on the same keys.
Z1Root    "Z1 root"      0 128 128  int 0 note             | Zone 1: the key that plays the wave unchanged; 128, Wave, takes each layer's own root from the wavetable (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the key at which zone 1 plays its sample at its original pitch, or lets the wave table decide.
    sound The root tunes the sample to the keyboard; if it is wrong, every note sounds out of tune.
Z1Tune    "Z1 tune"      0 96  48   int -48 st signed      | Zone 1: transposition
    how Transposes zone 1 by up to 48 semitones either way.
    sound Use it to move a sample up or down, or to layer an octave or a fifth.
Z1Fine    "Z1 fine"      0 2000 1000 lin -100 100 ct 1    | Zone 1: fine tune, in 0.1 cent steps
    how Detunes zone 1 by up to 100 cents in steps of 0.1 cent.
    sound A few cents between layered zones give a slow, warm beating.
Z1Level   "Z1 level"     0 600 480  db -48 12 inf          | Zone 1: level
    how Sets the level of zone 1, from -48 to +12 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance zones against each other.
Z1Pan     "Z1 pan"       0 200 100  lin -100 100 % 0       | Zone 1: pan (a stereo wave: balance)
    how Places zone 1 from 100 % left to 100 % right; a stereo wave is balanced instead.
    sound Panning zones apart widens layered sounds or spreads a drum kit.
Z1Start   "Z1 start"     0 65534 0  lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 1: where it starts, in % of the wave (the end, reversed)
    how Sets where zone 1 starts playing in the wave, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Moving the start skips a quiet or unwanted beginning and tightens the attack.
Z1End     "Z1 end"       0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 1: where it ends, in % of the wave (the start, reversed); it fades out over 2 ms before it
    how Sets where zone 1 stops playing in the wave, from 0 to 100 %; a short fade avoids a click.
    sound Moving the end trims off a tail, and an end before the start plays the wave backwards.
Z1Loop    "Z1 loop"      0 3   0    enum Wave Off Forward Ping-pong | Zone 1: Wave loops as the wavetable says (its loop points and type), Off plays through, Forward and Ping-pong loop between loop start and loop end
    how Chooses the loop mode of zone 1: as the wave says, off, forward or ping-pong.
    sound Looping holds a sound as long as the key is down, and ping-pong smooths the repeat by playing back and forth.
Z1LoopS   "Z1 loop start" 0 65534 0 lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 1: loop start, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 1 begins, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z1LoopE   "Z1 loop end"  0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 1: loop end, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 1 ends, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z1Xfade   "Z1 crossfade" 0 1000 215 pow 0 1 3 s 3          | Zone 1: a forward loop's crossfade (equal power), from the samples before loop start (after loop end, reversed); at most the loop's length and the room there is
    how Sets the length of the crossfade at the loop of zone 1, up to 1 second.
    sound A longer crossfade hides the jump where the loop restarts, and zero leaves a possible click.
Z1Trig    "Z1 trigger"   0 1   0    enum Gate One-shot     | Zone 1: Gate plays while the note is held, then releases; One-shot plays to the end and ignores note-offs and loops (Kit mode is one-shot)
    how Chooses whether zone 1 plays only while the key is held (Gate) or always to its end (One-shot).
    sound Gate suits sustained instruments, and One-shot suits drums and effects that should play out.
Z1Rev     "Z1 reverse"   0 1   0    switch                 | Zone 1: plays backwards, from its end to its start
    how Plays zone 1 backwards.
    sound Reversed samples swell into the note, which is useful for risers and transitions.
Z1Choke   "Z1 choke"     0 8   0    int 0                  | Zone 1: choke group 1–8 (0 off): a note in a group fades out, in 5 ms, every voice of the group still sounding (closed and open hats)
    how Puts zone 1 in one of eight choke groups, or none; a new note fades out the others in its group.
    sound Choke groups let a closed hat cut off an open hat, as on a real hat.

group Zone 2
