Z2VelLo   "Z2 vel low"   1 127 1    int 0                  | Zone 2: the lowest velocity it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the lowest velocity zone 2 responds to in Instrument mode.
    sound Zones with different velocity ranges give a soft layer and a hard layer on the same keys.
Z2VelHi   "Z2 vel high"  1 127 127  int 0                  | Zone 2: the highest velocity it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the highest velocity zone 2 responds to in Instrument mode.
    sound Zones with different velocity ranges give a soft layer and a hard layer on the same keys.
Z2Root    "Z2 root"      0 128 128  int 0 note             | Zone 2: the key that plays the wave unchanged; 128, Wave, takes each layer's own root from the wavetable (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the key at which zone 2 plays its sample at its original pitch, or lets the wave table decide.
    sound The root tunes the sample to the keyboard; if it is wrong, every note sounds out of tune.
Z2Tune    "Z2 tune"      0 96  48   int -48 st signed      | Zone 2: transposition
    how Transposes zone 2 by up to 48 semitones either way.
    sound Use it to move a sample up or down, or to layer an octave or a fifth.
Z2Fine    "Z2 fine"      0 2000 1000 lin -100 100 ct 1    | Zone 2: fine tune, in 0.1 cent steps
    how Detunes zone 2 by up to 100 cents in steps of 0.1 cent.
    sound A few cents between layered zones give a slow, warm beating.
Z2Level   "Z2 level"     0 600 480  db -48 12 inf          | Zone 2: level
    how Sets the level of zone 2, from -48 to +12 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance zones against each other.
Z2Pan     "Z2 pan"       0 200 100  lin -100 100 % 0       | Zone 2: pan (a stereo wave: balance)
    how Places zone 2 from 100 % left to 100 % right; a stereo wave is balanced instead.
    sound Panning zones apart widens layered sounds or spreads a drum kit.
Z2Start   "Z2 start"     0 65534 0  lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 2: where it starts, in % of the wave (the end, reversed)
    how Sets where zone 2 starts playing in the wave, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Moving the start skips a quiet or unwanted beginning and tightens the attack.
Z2End     "Z2 end"       0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 2: where it ends, in % of the wave (the start, reversed); it fades out over 2 ms before it
    how Sets where zone 2 stops playing in the wave, from 0 to 100 %; a short fade avoids a click.
    sound Moving the end trims off a tail, and an end before the start plays the wave backwards.
Z2Loop    "Z2 loop"      0 3   0    enum Wave Off Forward Ping-pong | Zone 2: Wave loops as the wavetable says (its loop points and type), Off plays through, Forward and Ping-pong loop between loop start and loop end
    how Chooses the loop mode of zone 2: as the wave says, off, forward or ping-pong.
    sound Looping holds a sound as long as the key is down, and ping-pong smooths the repeat by playing back and forth.
Z2LoopS   "Z2 loop start" 0 65534 0 lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 2: loop start, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 2 begins, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z2LoopE   "Z2 loop end"  0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 2: loop end, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 2 ends, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z2Xfade   "Z2 crossfade" 0 1000 215 pow 0 1 3 s 3          | Zone 2: a forward loop's crossfade (equal power), from the samples before loop start (after loop end, reversed); at most the loop's length and the room there is
    how Sets the length of the crossfade at the loop of zone 2, up to 1 second.
    sound A longer crossfade hides the jump where the loop restarts, and zero leaves a possible click.
Z2Trig    "Z2 trigger"   0 1   0    enum Gate One-shot     | Zone 2: Gate plays while the note is held, then releases; One-shot plays to the end and ignores note-offs and loops (Kit mode is one-shot)
    how Chooses whether zone 2 plays only while the key is held (Gate) or always to its end (One-shot).
    sound Gate suits sustained instruments, and One-shot suits drums and effects that should play out.
Z2Rev     "Z2 reverse"   0 1   0    switch                 | Zone 2: plays backwards, from its end to its start
    how Plays zone 2 backwards.
    sound Reversed samples swell into the note, which is useful for risers and transitions.
Z2Choke   "Z2 choke"     0 8   0    int 0                  | Zone 2: choke group 1–8 (0 off): a note in a group fades out, in 5 ms, every voice of the group still sounding (closed and open hats)
    how Puts zone 2 in one of eight choke groups, or none; a new note fades out the others in its group.
    sound Choke groups let a closed hat cut off an open hat, as on a real hat.

