Z4LoopS   "Z4 loop start" 0 65534 0 lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 4: loop start, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 4 begins, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z4LoopE   "Z4 loop end"  0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 4: loop end, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 4 ends, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z4Xfade   "Z4 crossfade" 0 1000 215 pow 0 1 3 s 3          | Zone 4: a forward loop's crossfade (equal power), from the samples before loop start (after loop end, reversed); at most the loop's length and the room there is
    how Sets the length of the crossfade at the loop of zone 4, up to 1 second.
    sound A longer crossfade hides the jump where the loop restarts, and zero leaves a possible click.
Z4Trig    "Z4 trigger"   0 1   0    enum Gate One-shot     | Zone 4: Gate plays while the note is held, then releases; One-shot plays to the end and ignores note-offs and loops (Kit mode is one-shot)
    how Chooses whether zone 4 plays only while the key is held (Gate) or always to its end (One-shot).
    sound Gate suits sustained instruments, and One-shot suits drums and effects that should play out.
Z4Rev     "Z4 reverse"   0 1   0    switch                 | Zone 4: plays backwards, from its end to its start
    how Plays zone 4 backwards.
    sound Reversed samples swell into the note, which is useful for risers and transitions.
Z4Choke   "Z4 choke"     0 8   0    int 0                  | Zone 4: choke group 1–8 (0 off): a note in a group fades out, in 5 ms, every voice of the group still sounding (closed and open hats)
    how Puts zone 4 in one of eight choke groups, or none; a new note fades out the others in its group.
    sound Choke groups let a closed hat cut off an open hat, as on a real hat.

group Zone 5
Z5Wave    "Z5 wave"      0 254 0    int 0 wave            | Zone 5's wave: 0 off, 1–200 a slot of the song's wavetable (wave_import), 201 on a built-in sample (the manual lists them)
    how Chooses the sound zone 5 plays: off, a wave slot of the song, or a built-in sample.
    sound The wave is the raw material of the zone; each slot or sample has its own character.
Z5KeyLo   "Z5 key low"   0 127 0    int 0 note             | Zone 5: the lowest key it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the lowest key zone 5 plays in Instrument mode.
    sound Together with the high key it decides which part of the keyboard triggers this zone.
Z5KeyHi   "Z5 key high"  0 127 127  int 0 note             | Zone 5: the highest key it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the highest key zone 5 plays in Instrument mode.
    sound Together with the low key it decides which part of the keyboard triggers this zone.
Z5VelLo   "Z5 vel low"   1 127 1    int 0                  | Zone 5: the lowest velocity it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the lowest velocity zone 5 responds to in Instrument mode.
    sound Zones with different velocity ranges give a soft layer and a hard layer on the same keys.
Z5VelHi   "Z5 vel high"  1 127 127  int 0                  | Zone 5: the highest velocity it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the highest velocity zone 5 responds to in Instrument mode.
    sound Zones with different velocity ranges give a soft layer and a hard layer on the same keys.
Z5Root    "Z5 root"      0 128 128  int 0 note             | Zone 5: the key that plays the wave unchanged; 128, Wave, takes each layer's own root from the wavetable (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the key at which zone 5 plays its sample at its original pitch, or lets the wave table decide.
    sound The root tunes the sample to the keyboard; if it is wrong, every note sounds out of tune.
Z5Tune    "Z5 tune"      0 96  48   int -48 st signed      | Zone 5: transposition
    how Transposes zone 5 by up to 48 semitones either way.
    sound Use it to move a sample up or down, or to layer an octave or a fifth.
Z5Fine    "Z5 fine"      0 2000 1000 lin -100 100 ct 1    | Zone 5: fine tune, in 0.1 cent steps
    how Detunes zone 5 by up to 100 cents in steps of 0.1 cent.
    sound A few cents between layered zones give a slow, warm beating.
Z5Level   "Z5 level"     0 600 480  db -48 12 inf          | Zone 5: level
    how Sets the level of zone 5, from -48 to +12 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance zones against each other.
Z5Pan     "Z5 pan"       0 200 100  lin -100 100 % 0       | Zone 5: pan (a stereo wave: balance)
    how Places zone 5 from 100 % left to 100 % right; a stereo wave is balanced instead.
    sound Panning zones apart widens layered sounds or spreads a drum kit.
Z5Start   "Z5 start"     0 65534 0  lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 5: where it starts, in % of the wave (the end, reversed)
    how Sets where zone 5 starts playing in the wave, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Moving the start skips a quiet or unwanted beginning and tightens the attack.
Z5End     "Z5 end"       0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 5: where it ends, in % of the wave (the start, reversed); it fades out over 2 ms before it
    how Sets where zone 5 stops playing in the wave, from 0 to 100 %; a short fade avoids a click.
    sound Moving the end trims off a tail, and an end before the start plays the wave backwards.
Z5Loop    "Z5 loop"      0 3   0    enum Wave Off Forward Ping-pong | Zone 5: Wave loops as the wavetable says (its loop points and type), Off plays through, Forward and Ping-pong loop between loop start and loop end
    how Chooses the loop mode of zone 5: as the wave says, off, forward or ping-pong.
    sound Looping holds a sound as long as the key is down, and ping-pong smooths the repeat by playing back and forth.
Z5LoopS   "Z5 loop start" 0 65534 0 lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 5: loop start, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 5 begins, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z5LoopE   "Z5 loop end"  0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 5: loop end, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 5 ends, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z5Xfade   "Z5 crossfade" 0 1000 215 pow 0 1 3 s 3          | Zone 5: a forward loop's crossfade (equal power), from the samples before loop start (after loop end, reversed); at most the loop's length and the room there is
    how Sets the length of the crossfade at the loop of zone 5, up to 1 second.
    sound A longer crossfade hides the jump where the loop restarts, and zero leaves a possible click.
Z5Trig    "Z5 trigger"   0 1   0    enum Gate One-shot     | Zone 5: Gate plays while the note is held, then releases; One-shot plays to the end and ignores note-offs and loops (Kit mode is one-shot)
    how Chooses whether zone 5 plays only while the key is held (Gate) or always to its end (One-shot).
    sound Gate suits sustained instruments, and One-shot suits drums and effects that should play out.
Z5Rev     "Z5 reverse"   0 1   0    switch                 | Zone 5: plays backwards, from its end to its start
    how Plays zone 5 backwards.
    sound Reversed samples swell into the note, which is useful for risers and transitions.
Z5Choke   "Z5 choke"     0 8   0    int 0                  | Zone 5: choke group 1–8 (0 off): a note in a group fades out, in 5 ms, every voice of the group still sounding (closed and open hats)
    how Puts zone 5 in one of eight choke groups, or none; a new note fades out the others in its group.
    sound Choke groups let a closed hat cut off an open hat, as on a real hat.

