    sound Moving the end trims off a tail, and an end before the start plays the wave backwards.
Z9Loop    "Z9 loop"      0 3   0    enum Wave Off Forward Ping-pong | Zone 9: Wave loops as the wavetable says (its loop points and type), Off plays through, Forward and Ping-pong loop between loop start and loop end
    how Chooses the loop mode of zone 9: as the wave says, off, forward or ping-pong.
    sound Looping holds a sound as long as the key is down, and ping-pong smooths the repeat by playing back and forth.
Z9LoopS   "Z9 loop start" 0 65534 0 lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 9: loop start, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 9 begins, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z9LoopE   "Z9 loop end"  0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 9: loop end, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 9 ends, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z9Xfade   "Z9 crossfade" 0 1000 215 pow 0 1 3 s 3          | Zone 9: a forward loop's crossfade (equal power), from the samples before loop start (after loop end, reversed); at most the loop's length and the room there is
    how Sets the length of the crossfade at the loop of zone 9, up to 1 second.
    sound A longer crossfade hides the jump where the loop restarts, and zero leaves a possible click.
Z9Trig    "Z9 trigger"   0 1   0    enum Gate One-shot     | Zone 9: Gate plays while the note is held, then releases; One-shot plays to the end and ignores note-offs and loops (Kit mode is one-shot)
    how Chooses whether zone 9 plays only while the key is held (Gate) or always to its end (One-shot).
    sound Gate suits sustained instruments, and One-shot suits drums and effects that should play out.
Z9Rev     "Z9 reverse"   0 1   0    switch                 | Zone 9: plays backwards, from its end to its start
    how Plays zone 9 backwards.
    sound Reversed samples swell into the note, which is useful for risers and transitions.
Z9Choke   "Z9 choke"     0 8   0    int 0                  | Zone 9: choke group 1–8 (0 off): a note in a group fades out, in 5 ms, every voice of the group still sounding (closed and open hats)
    how Puts zone 9 in one of eight choke groups, or none; a new note fades out the others in its group.
    sound Choke groups let a closed hat cut off an open hat, as on a real hat.

group Zone 10
Z10Wave    "Z10 wave"      0 254 0    int 0 wave            | Zone 10's wave: 0 off, 1–200 a slot of the song's wavetable (wave_import), 201 on a built-in sample (the manual lists them)
    how Chooses the sound zone 10 plays: off, a wave slot of the song, or a built-in sample.
    sound The wave is the raw material of the zone; each slot or sample has its own character.
Z10KeyLo   "Z10 key low"   0 127 0    int 0 note             | Zone 10: the lowest key it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the lowest key zone 10 plays in Instrument mode.
    sound Together with the high key it decides which part of the keyboard triggers this zone.
Z10KeyHi   "Z10 key high"  0 127 127  int 0 note             | Zone 10: the highest key it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the highest key zone 10 plays in Instrument mode.
    sound Together with the low key it decides which part of the keyboard triggers this zone.
Z10VelLo   "Z10 vel low"   1 127 1    int 0                  | Zone 10: the lowest velocity it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the lowest velocity zone 10 responds to in Instrument mode.
    sound Zones with different velocity ranges give a soft layer and a hard layer on the same keys.
Z10VelHi   "Z10 vel high"  1 127 127  int 0                  | Zone 10: the highest velocity it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the highest velocity zone 10 responds to in Instrument mode.
    sound Zones with different velocity ranges give a soft layer and a hard layer on the same keys.
Z10Root    "Z10 root"      0 128 128  int 0 note             | Zone 10: the key that plays the wave unchanged; 128, Wave, takes each layer's own root from the wavetable (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the key at which zone 10 plays its sample at its original pitch, or lets the wave table decide.
    sound The root tunes the sample to the keyboard; if it is wrong, every note sounds out of tune.
Z10Tune    "Z10 tune"      0 96  48   int -48 st signed      | Zone 10: transposition
    how Transposes zone 10 by up to 48 semitones either way.
    sound Use it to move a sample up or down, or to layer an octave or a fifth.
Z10Fine    "Z10 fine"      0 2000 1000 lin -100 100 ct 1    | Zone 10: fine tune, in 0.1 cent steps
    how Detunes zone 10 by up to 100 cents in steps of 0.1 cent.
    sound A few cents between layered zones give a slow, warm beating.
Z10Level   "Z10 level"     0 600 480  db -48 12 inf          | Zone 10: level
    how Sets the level of zone 10, from -48 to +12 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance zones against each other.
Z10Pan     "Z10 pan"       0 200 100  lin -100 100 % 0       | Zone 10: pan (a stereo wave: balance)
    how Places zone 10 from 100 % left to 100 % right; a stereo wave is balanced instead.
    sound Panning zones apart widens layered sounds or spreads a drum kit.
Z10Start   "Z10 start"     0 65534 0  lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 10: where it starts, in % of the wave (the end, reversed)
    how Sets where zone 10 starts playing in the wave, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Moving the start skips a quiet or unwanted beginning and tightens the attack.
Z10End     "Z10 end"       0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 10: where it ends, in % of the wave (the start, reversed); it fades out over 2 ms before it
    how Sets where zone 10 stops playing in the wave, from 0 to 100 %; a short fade avoids a click.
    sound Moving the end trims off a tail, and an end before the start plays the wave backwards.
Z10Loop    "Z10 loop"      0 3   0    enum Wave Off Forward Ping-pong | Zone 10: Wave loops as the wavetable says (its loop points and type), Off plays through, Forward and Ping-pong loop between loop start and loop end
    how Chooses the loop mode of zone 10: as the wave says, off, forward or ping-pong.
    sound Looping holds a sound as long as the key is down, and ping-pong smooths the repeat by playing back and forth.
Z10LoopS   "Z10 loop start" 0 65534 0 lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 10: loop start, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 10 begins, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z10LoopE   "Z10 loop end"  0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 10: loop end, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 10 ends, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z10Xfade   "Z10 crossfade" 0 1000 215 pow 0 1 3 s 3          | Zone 10: a forward loop's crossfade (equal power), from the samples before loop start (after loop end, reversed); at most the loop's length and the room there is
    how Sets the length of the crossfade at the loop of zone 10, up to 1 second.
    sound A longer crossfade hides the jump where the loop restarts, and zero leaves a possible click.
Z10Trig    "Z10 trigger"   0 1   0    enum Gate One-shot     | Zone 10: Gate plays while the note is held, then releases; One-shot plays to the end and ignores note-offs and loops (Kit mode is one-shot)
    how Chooses whether zone 10 plays only while the key is held (Gate) or always to its end (One-shot).
    sound Gate suits sustained instruments, and One-shot suits drums and effects that should play out.
Z10Rev     "Z10 reverse"   0 1   0    switch                 | Zone 10: plays backwards, from its end to its start
    how Plays zone 10 backwards.
    sound Reversed samples swell into the note, which is useful for risers and transitions.
Z10Choke   "Z10 choke"     0 8   0    int 0                  | Zone 10: choke group 1–8 (0 off): a note in a group fades out, in 5 ms, every voice of the group still sounding (closed and open hats)
    how Puts zone 10 in one of eight choke groups, or none; a new note fades out the others in its group.
    sound Choke groups let a closed hat cut off an open hat, as on a real hat.

