Z14Pan     "Z14 pan"       0 200 100  lin -100 100 % 0       | Zone 14: pan (a stereo wave: balance)
    how Places zone 14 from 100 % left to 100 % right; a stereo wave is balanced instead.
    sound Panning zones apart widens layered sounds or spreads a drum kit.
Z14Start   "Z14 start"     0 65534 0  lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 14: where it starts, in % of the wave (the end, reversed)
    how Sets where zone 14 starts playing in the wave, from 0 to 100 %.
    sound Moving the start skips a quiet or unwanted beginning and tightens the attack.
Z14End     "Z14 end"       0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 14: where it ends, in % of the wave (the start, reversed); it fades out over 2 ms before it
    how Sets where zone 14 stops playing in the wave, from 0 to 100 %; a short fade avoids a click.
    sound Moving the end trims off a tail, and an end before the start plays the wave backwards.
Z14Loop    "Z14 loop"      0 3   0    enum Wave Off Forward Ping-pong | Zone 14: Wave loops as the wavetable says (its loop points and type), Off plays through, Forward and Ping-pong loop between loop start and loop end
    how Chooses the loop mode of zone 14: as the wave says, off, forward or ping-pong.
    sound Looping holds a sound as long as the key is down, and ping-pong smooths the repeat by playing back and forth.
Z14LoopS   "Z14 loop start" 0 65534 0 lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 14: loop start, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 14 begins, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z14LoopE   "Z14 loop end"  0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 14: loop end, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 14 ends, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z14Xfade   "Z14 crossfade" 0 1000 215 pow 0 1 3 s 3          | Zone 14: a forward loop's crossfade (equal power), from the samples before loop start (after loop end, reversed); at most the loop's length and the room there is
    how Sets the length of the crossfade at the loop of zone 14, up to 1 second.
    sound A longer crossfade hides the jump where the loop restarts, and zero leaves a possible click.
Z14Trig    "Z14 trigger"   0 1   0    enum Gate One-shot     | Zone 14: Gate plays while the note is held, then releases; One-shot plays to the end and ignores note-offs and loops (Kit mode is one-shot)
    how Chooses whether zone 14 plays only while the key is held (Gate) or always to its end (One-shot).
    sound Gate suits sustained instruments, and One-shot suits drums and effects that should play out.
Z14Rev     "Z14 reverse"   0 1   0    switch                 | Zone 14: plays backwards, from its end to its start
    how Plays zone 14 backwards.
    sound Reversed samples swell into the note, which is useful for risers and transitions.
Z14Choke   "Z14 choke"     0 8   0    int 0                  | Zone 14: choke group 1–8 (0 off): a note in a group fades out, in 5 ms, every voice of the group still sounding (closed and open hats)
    how Puts zone 14 in one of eight choke groups, or none; a new note fades out the others in its group.
    sound Choke groups let a closed hat cut off an open hat, as on a real hat.

group Zone 15
Z15Wave    "Z15 wave"      0 254 0    int 0 wave            | Zone 15's wave: 0 off, 1–200 a slot of the song's wavetable (wave_import), 201 on a built-in sample (the manual lists them)
    how Chooses the sound zone 15 plays: off, a wave slot of the song, or a built-in sample.
    sound The wave is the raw material of the zone; each slot or sample has its own character.
Z15KeyLo   "Z15 key low"   0 127 0    int 0 note             | Zone 15: the lowest key it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the lowest key zone 15 plays in Instrument mode.
    sound Together with the high key it decides which part of the keyboard triggers this zone.
Z15KeyHi   "Z15 key high"  0 127 127  int 0 note             | Zone 15: the highest key it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the highest key zone 15 plays in Instrument mode.
    sound Together with the low key it decides which part of the keyboard triggers this zone.
Z15VelLo   "Z15 vel low"   1 127 1    int 0                  | Zone 15: the lowest velocity it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the lowest velocity zone 15 responds to in Instrument mode.
    sound Zones with different velocity ranges give a soft layer and a hard layer on the same keys.
Z15VelHi   "Z15 vel high"  1 127 127  int 0                  | Zone 15: the highest velocity it plays (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the highest velocity zone 15 responds to in Instrument mode.
    sound Zones with different velocity ranges give a soft layer and a hard layer on the same keys.
Z15Root    "Z15 root"      0 128 128  int 0 note             | Zone 15: the key that plays the wave unchanged; 128, Wave, takes each layer's own root from the wavetable (Instrument mode)
    how Sets the key at which zone 15 plays its sample at its original pitch, or lets the wave table decide.
    sound The root tunes the sample to the keyboard; if it is wrong, every note sounds out of tune.
Z15Tune    "Z15 tune"      0 96  48   int -48 st signed      | Zone 15: transposition
    how Transposes zone 15 by up to 48 semitones either way.
    sound Use it to move a sample up or down, or to layer an octave or a fifth.
Z15Fine    "Z15 fine"      0 2000 1000 lin -100 100 ct 1    | Zone 15: fine tune, in 0.1 cent steps
    how Detunes zone 15 by up to 100 cents in steps of 0.1 cent.
    sound A few cents between layered zones give a slow, warm beating.
Z15Level   "Z15 level"     0 600 480  db -48 12 inf          | Zone 15: level
    how Sets the level of zone 15, from -48 to +12 dB, or off.
    sound Use it to balance zones against each other.
Z15Pan     "Z15 pan"       0 200 100  lin -100 100 % 0       | Zone 15: pan (a stereo wave: balance)
    how Places zone 15 from 100 % left to 100 % right; a stereo wave is balanced instead.
    sound Panning zones apart widens layered sounds or spreads a drum kit.
Z15Start   "Z15 start"     0 65534 0  lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 15: where it starts, in % of the wave (the end, reversed)
