    sound Moving the start skips a quiet or unwanted beginning and tightens the attack.
Z15End     "Z15 end"       0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 15: where it ends, in % of the wave (the start, reversed); it fades out over 2 ms before it
    how Sets where zone 15 stops playing in the wave, from 0 to 100 %; a short fade avoids a click.
    sound Moving the end trims off a tail, and an end before the start plays the wave backwards.
Z15Loop    "Z15 loop"      0 3   0    enum Wave Off Forward Ping-pong | Zone 15: Wave loops as the wavetable says (its loop points and type), Off plays through, Forward and Ping-pong loop between loop start and loop end
    how Chooses the loop mode of zone 15: as the wave says, off, forward or ping-pong.
    sound Looping holds a sound as long as the key is down, and ping-pong smooths the repeat by playing back and forth.
Z15LoopS   "Z15 loop start" 0 65534 0 lin 0 100 % 3          | Zone 15: loop start, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 15 begins, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z15LoopE   "Z15 loop end"  0 65534 65534 lin 0 100 % 3       | Zone 15: loop end, in % of the wave (Forward, Ping-pong)
    how Sets where the loop of zone 15 ends, from 0 to 100 % of the wave.
    sound The loop points decide which part of the sample repeats while a note is held.
Z15Xfade   "Z15 crossfade" 0 1000 215 pow 0 1 3 s 3          | Zone 15: a forward loop's crossfade (equal power), from the samples before loop start (after loop end, reversed); at most the loop's length and the room there is
    how Sets the length of the crossfade at the loop of zone 15, up to 1 second.
    sound A longer crossfade hides the jump where the loop restarts, and zero leaves a possible click.
Z15Trig    "Z15 trigger"   0 1   0    enum Gate One-shot     | Zone 15: Gate plays while the note is held, then releases; One-shot plays to the end and ignores note-offs and loops (Kit mode is one-shot)
    how Chooses whether zone 15 plays only while the key is held (Gate) or always to its end (One-shot).
    sound Gate suits sustained instruments, and One-shot suits drums and effects that should play out.
Z15Rev     "Z15 reverse"   0 1   0    switch                 | Zone 15: plays backwards, from its end to its start
    how Plays zone 15 backwards.
    sound Reversed samples swell into the note, which is useful for risers and transitions.
Z15Choke   "Z15 choke"     0 8   0    int 0                  | Zone 15: choke group 1–8 (0 off): a note in a group fades out, in 5 ms, every voice of the group still sounding (closed and open hats)
    how Puts zone 15 in one of eight choke groups, or none; a new note fades out the others in its group.
